---
import "../styles/global.css"
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro"
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro"
import GtagHead from "../components/GtagHead.astro"
import NotifuseAnalytics from "../components/NotifuseAnalytics.astro"
import WorkspacesPreview from "../components/WorkspacesPreview.astro"
import PermissionsPreview from "../components/PermissionsPreview.astro"
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>Multi-entity networks & franchises - Notifuse</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="One email platform for a whole network: headquarters sets templates, translations and permissions; each franchise or entity keeps its own isolated workspace, domain and sending reputation."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://notifuse.com/networks" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <GtagHead />
    <NotifuseAnalytics />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-white-98 text-slate-900">
    <div class="container relative border-r border-l border-gray-200">
      <Navigation />

      <main>
        <section class="pt-28 pb-16 px-4 lg:px-8">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
              One email platform for the whole network
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
              Headquarters keeps control of the brand. Every franchise, store or entity
              sends from its own isolated workspace — its own contacts, domain and sending
              reputation.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center">
              <a href="https://demo.notifuse.com/console/signin?email=demo@notifuse.com" class="bg-primary text-white px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">See the live interface</a>
              <a href="/pricing/self-hosted" class="border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-white transition-colors">See licences</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The problem with one shared account</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              A network usually ends up with one of two bad options. Either every entity
              shares one marketing account — one badly targeted campaign can damage the
              sending reputation of the whole network, and nobody can tell who sent what.
              Or every entity buys its own tool — headquarters loses the brand, the
              templates and any common view of what is being sent.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              Notifuse is built for the middle: one deployment, many isolated workspaces,
              governed from the centre.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Headquarters sets the frame</h2>
              <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
                Templates and their translations are prepared centrally, so every entity
                sends on-brand email in its own language. Permissions decide who can do
                what in each workspace: a local manager runs their campaigns, headquarters
                keeps the settings and the integrations.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-700">
                Each workspace has its own database, contacts, campaigns and custom domain
                for tracking and unsubscribe pages. Entities do not see each other's data.
              </p>
            </div>
            <WorkspacesPreview />
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
            <PermissionsPreview />
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">One entity's mistake stays its own</h2>
              <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
                With Amazon SES tenant isolation, each entity can send under its own
                reputation and suppression list. A campaign that goes wrong in one store
                can be paused there — it does not take the rest of the network down with
                it.
              </p>
              <p class="text-gray-700">
                And because workspaces are isolated, a local team can be given exactly the
                access it needs, and no more.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">An example</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-3">Illustrative scenario — not a customer case.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              A retail network with 40 locations deploys Notifuse once, on its own
              servers. Headquarters prepares the templates and the two languages the
              network uses. Each store gets a workspace with its own contacts and its own
              domain, and sends its local campaigns. Headquarters can see the frame it
              set; stores cannot see each other's lists. When the network grows past the
              workspaces in its licence, it moves to a Custom licence instead of changing
              tools.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700">
              Access is governed with single sign-on and granular permissions, and admin
              actions are kept in audit logs. Details are on our
              {" "}<a href="/security" class="text-primary hover:underline">security page</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-16 px-4 lg:px-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Licences for networks</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
              Start free with three workspaces. Studio covers five, Agency and Enterprise
              fifteen — with permissions, SES tenant isolation and template translations,
              plus single sign-on and audit logs on Enterprise. More than fifteen
              workspaces, or a network-wide rollout? That is a
              {" "}<a href="/pricing/self-hosted#custom" class="text-primary hover:underline">Custom licence</a>,
              quoted per deployment.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
              Paid licences include private email support, Monday to Friday — first reply
              within two business days, one when production is blocked.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <a href="/pricing/self-hosted" class="bg-primary text-white px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors">Compare licences</a>
              <a href="mailto:hello@notifuse.com?subject=Custom%20licence%20—%20network" class="border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 px-6 py-2.5 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-white transition-colors">Talk about a Custom licence</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>

      <Footer />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
